fauna of the area.  Clovers grow in clumps nearby beside a few sunflowers.  To

the south a line of trees marks the edge of a forest, the nearly impenetrable

wall of oaks and elms stretching to the east and west around a small pond to

the north.  The greenish water's south shore here is lined with wet, slimy

rocks which looks extremely slippery and yet should not be too hard to cross.

"
"cattaills, etc, mossy rocks, lily pads

mosquitoes, dragonflies, deer flies, horse flies

