house.  Bits of glass and fabric lie strewn on the ground near what were large

windows.  The house itself is most massive, and built of light grey stone.  It

is surrounded by a low green shrub, the trimming of which must have been the

full-time job of at least one gardener.  A large wooden door once sealed the

house from the outside world; now it looks like it barely can stay on its

hinges.  A large path leads east-west from the house, bordered by lovely fruit

trees.

"
